		}
		{
			description: [
				"Distilled Bifrost converts into the entry currency of five other magical traditions."
				""
				"YIELDS: 6x mana powder, 3x source gem, 2x otherworld essence, 4x arcane essence, 4x gold leaf, 1x mana pearl."
				""
				"THE RATES ARE POOR AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. This is a foothold in a discipline you have not studied, not a way to skip studying it. What it buys you is the chance to begin somewhere new without beginning from nothing."
				""
				"Only one conversion reaches past a system's entry tier, and it costs four."
			]
			icon: "botania:mana_powder"
			id: "6CA5D7B61FA3C498"
			optional: true
			shape: "gear"
			subtitle: "One material, every road"
			tasks: [{
				id: "06431F061B92D647"
				title: "The Exchange"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			title: "The Exchange"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 2.5d
		}
		{
			description: [
				"A heated Create mixer will make Liquid Bifrost from things that grow back."
				""
				"RECIPE: 2 crystal shards + 1 mana powder + 500mB water -> 250mB Liquid Bifrost."
				"STATION: Basin with a Mechanical Mixer, heated."
				""
				"WHY IT IS RENEWABLE: six of the seven crystals have a budding block and regrow forever. The shard tag holds exactly those six -- frost does not bud and is not in it. Water is water. Mana powder is a flower."
				""
				"It is NOT cheaper than finding a pool and was never meant to be. Four mixes to the bucket. It is only endless, which is a different and better property."
				""
				"Era VII because that is the first era that teaches the mixer."
			]
			icon: "create:basin"
